        <mxCell id="UhXnpPRqJG6slf9-OY_N-6" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fa6800;strokeColor=#C73500;fontColor=#000000;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ffffff&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Run GMM on controls w/out chrx and fit a LMM with ns() and random intercept-only model to use as features in GMM&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;2,025 CpGs were identified has having essentially zero variability (SD&amp;lt;1e8). In other words, the subject level intercepts showed little to no variability. These were lumped into group 1 (unimodal group).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ffffff&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
